// The B deck — backbeat. It lands on the crossfade's `b` port, which is why its chain ends
// there and it runs no modules of its own.
//
// BYPASSED on purpose, in chains.yaml, and this is the one thing about the demo worth reading
// twice.
//
// `out` compiles as a PARALLEL path in this compiler — that is what makes a send a send, the
// dry signal carrying on to the master beside it. A deck feeding only a crossfade's second port
// gets the same treatment, so unbypassed you hear deck B twice: once raw, once through the
// module, and pushing Mix to 0 does not take it away.
//
// Bypassing a LANE says "this lane is not heard on its own" — on a source, bypass means it
// produces nothing rather than passing something through. It works because Tracktion's muting
// node deliberately still lets clips through to aux sends and sidechains, so the crossfade keeps
// its second signal while the master stops getting a duplicate. Measured: with it, Mix 0 is the
// kick alone, Mix 1 the snare alone; without it, the snare is there at every setting. See
// packages/song/docs/ports.md.
//
// TODO: try automating Mix so the two decks trade places over a bar.
extends("@meta/track")
events([ref("snare").start("1:2:1"), ref("snare").start("1:4:1")])
